From 7e86515d20d10c12e972306e74e3695ac889108e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 16:21:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arifi-sync: x1i-reword - trailer table and replay script for
 the 58 post-x1i commits

provenance --strict fails on 58 integ commits after the shipped engine 9c01a28321: none carries
Origin/Taken-from and none carries Measured-effect. integ is unpublished, so these are repaired, not
exempted. post-x1i-trailers.tsv gives each fork sha its Origin (ArifiLabs native + lane) and
Measured-effect: 34 from the 2026-10-05 release ledger Table 1/2 (matched by patch-id of the
ledger's fork commits), 4 from the number in the commit's own subject, 20 UNMEASURED.

reword.py is run by lane 298 at merge freeze. It never rewrites the fork in place: it clones the
branch, replays 9c01a28321..tip with commit-tree (same trees, identities and dates), adds only the
missing trailers via interpret-trailers, re-keys full shas in tools/arifi-sync/**/*.json, and
fetches the result back as release-prep/reword-out. Then: reset --keep release-prep/reword-out in
the integ worktree, and series regen. It refuses a merge in range and a table sha outside it.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release engineering for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Origin: release-prep (HQ82)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - release tooling only; no inference code path is touched. Dry run on a scratch clone of release/prep: 60 commits replayed, 58 reworded, 60 shas changed, trees identical.
